      "side": 1,
      "message": "On CQ run RustALL CQ run was failing due to a crash. The crash was caused at the Rust/C++ FFI boundary in the Rust JPEG reader setup path. We were returning a boxed wrapper result object, unwrapping it in C++, and then dropping that wrapper; on truncated-input test flow this hit an invalid free path (PartitionAlloc trap), which is why RustALL dm crashed.\n\nFix:\nI simplified the FFI contract so `new_reader` now returns the Reader directly (no wrapper result object to unwrap/drop), and updated both C++ call sites (initial decode and rewind) to use that direct return. We also kept the safer explicit stream-read loop in the Rust FFI reader path as additional hardening for partial/truncated input handling.\n\nValidation:\nLocal RustALL dm run (including RustJpeg) now passes, the specific `RustJpegCodec_incomplete_input` regression test passes, and presubmit passes.\n\nCan you help queueing CQ again on latest changes?\n\nThanks!",
